  "final_text": "**None of the eleven files works as evidence for R7.** As of today, R7 is a **GAP**.\n\nR7 asks for: *\"A restore test of your backups from the last 12 months, with its result.\"* Tannwald's rules: the document must be dated on or after 10 December 2025, it must name its owner, and *\"A description of what you do is not enough. Send the record that shows it was done.\"*\n\nI checked every file that mentions backups or restores:\n\n| File | Quote | QUOTE | PERIOD | SCOPE | APPROVAL | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| backup-report_2026-10.txt | \"Restore test: not done in 2026. Planned for Q4 2026 (owner: IT lead).\" | ✗ shows no test was done; \"planned\" isn't evidence | ✓ generated 2026-11-01 | ✗ covers only \"Servicepult export, file share\" | ✓ owner: IT lead | **GAP**: the file shows R7 isn't met |\n| it-notes_2026-10-06.md | \"Backups are tested, the jobs run every night.\" | ✗ a statement, not a record | ✓ 2026-10-06 | – | ✗ \"Not reviewed by anyone.\" | doesn't count |\n| infosec-policy_v3_FINAL.md | \"Backups are restore-tested twice a year.\" | ✗ a rule, not proof it happened | ✗ approved 2024-03-12, review was due March 2025 | – | ✓ Managing Director | doesn't count |\n| infosec-policy_v4_DRAFT.md | \"Rules 1 to 5 as in version 3.\" | ✗ a rule | – | – | ✗ \"Approved by: (open)\" | doesn't count |\n| subprocessors_2026-09.csv | \"Nordlager GmbH,file share and backups\" | ✗ only names the backup provider | – | – | – | doesn't count |\n\n**Before you send anything:**\n- **The backup report works against you.** You can send it to be open with Tannwald, but it doesn't answer R7. It shows the policy's twice-a-year restore test hasn't happened in 2026. It also covers only the Servicepult export and the file share, not Sprechband (call recordings) or Claude Team.\n- **Don't send the IT notes as evidence.** \"Backups are tested\" contradicts the backup report, and nobody has reviewed the notes. If they go to Tannwald, they undermine the rest of what you send.\n- **10–31 December 2025** isn't covered by any file, so it has no evidence either way.\n\n**What would close the gap:** a restore test record with the date, the systems or data restored, the result (success or failure, and time taken), and who ran it. It has to be dated before the 25 November deadline. A real test run now would count, because it falls inside the 12-month window. The IT lead owns this.\n\n**Draft note to the IT lead:**\n> Tannwald's R7 asks for \"a restore test of your backups from the last 12 months, with its result,\" as a record, not a description. Our October backup report says \"Restore test: not done in 2026.\" Your notes say backups are tested. Is there a restore test record from 10 Dec 2025 onwards? If not, can you run one before 25 Nov and record the date, systems restored, result and who ran it? Please also say whether Sprechband recordings are backed up at all. \"There is no test record\" is a perfectly good answer; we just need to know before we reply.\n\nWhether to send the backup report anyway, along with a short note that a test is scheduled, is up to you.",
